      "content": "exactly. and it's not just the time. the trucks they use aren't even standard utility trucks, they're those heavy, unmarked white ones with lots of specialized sensor equipment on the back. i saw one last night and it looked more like surveillance tech than a water wrench. if they're trying to map out vibrations or footfalls in our houses, what kind of data would they be collecting and why wouldn't they just use satellites or something instead of digging under our street?",
